>> title: Tabbouleh
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: bulgur, parsley, levantine, salad, no-cook
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: tabouli, tabbouli, taboule, tabouleh
>> pairs-with: hummus, baba-ganoush
>> servings: 6
>> time: 40 min
>> step.1: soak 20 min, fluff
>> step.2: whisk
>> step.3: toss
>> step.4: fold in, rest 15 min

Soak @fine bulgur{1/2%cup}(90 g) in @cold water{2/3%cup}(160 mL) for ~{20%min}, then fluff with a #fork{}.

Whisk @lemon juice{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @extra-virgin olive oil{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @kosher salt{1%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp} in a #large bowl{}.

Toss @&(~1)dressing{} with @flat-leaf parsley{3%cups}(finely chopped, from about 3 bunches), @mint{1/2%cup}(finely chopped), @scallions{4}(thinly sliced), and @plum tomatoes{2}(seeded and diced).

Fold @&(~3)bulgur{} into @&(~1)salad{} and rest ~{15%min} before serving.
